AB  - Artificial Intelligence has gained significant momentum in driving cybersecurity innovations over the past half decade.Increasingly, specialized language models for cybersecurity applications in malware analysis, anti-phishing, program repair, and more have gained substantial traction.This minitrack focuses on providing a venue for researchers to share work on the intersection of AI and Cybersecurity with emphasis on collaborative inter-organizational realms, shared collaborative domains, or with collaborative technologies.Three papers were accepted to this year's minitrack, focusing on topics related to malicious attack channels, extracting protected health information from multi-lingual hacker communities, and surveying language models for real-time threat detection.
